orrection and no billing-integrity referral.\n\nRIDER INSTRUCTION (POL-RD-04). The chat log (EV-CHAT-02805) holds 0 messages with no timestamps. There is no rider instruction and no waypoint_hint, so no distance could be excluded and the leg is simply unavailable on this record.\n\nTRAFFIC ADVISORY AND UNCITED ASSERTIONS (POL-RD-13, POL-RD-08). EV-ADVIS-02805-01 is MISSING: its payload is null, its weight_multiplier is 0.0 and it carries the blocking issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — no advisory covers the Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3 corridor in this window. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run and any external-cause assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. In the event, the driver's statement cites no evidence ID and asserts no traffic cause, so it is an assertion that carries no weight and no exoneration was required of him, since no deviation was established against him. No exculpatory clause was invoked by the driver against a cited missing artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged: the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it.\n\nPROFILE COUNTERS (POL-RD-06, POL-RD-08, POL-GEN-01). On the only fields POL-RD-06 permits, deviation_flags_90d is 0 and completed_trips_90d is 172 (EV-DPROF-02805), so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is available. On the rider's side, deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0 (EV-RPROF-02805), so the serial-claimant corroboration requirement in POL-RD-08 is not engaged. Lifetime counters such as prior_deviation_flags, and other profile fields such as rating, account age and cancellation rate, are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used as any ground of decision; both advocates' claims citing prior_deviation_flags did so only to disclaim it, and nothing was discarded on that account.\n\nESCALATION (POL-RD-10). No trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; trip identifiers match across trip_record